=== COMMON EMITTER AMPLIFIER DESIGN ===
Project: Electronics Circuit Design
Course & Section: Computer Engineering – COE3A

1. COMPONENTS:
   - Q1: 2N3904 NPN Transistor
   - R1: 10 kΩ
   - R2: 2.2 kΩ
   - Rc: 2.2 kΩ
   - Re: 470 Ω
   - C1, C2: 10 µF
   - Ce: 100 µF
   - Vcc: 12 V DC

2. CALCULATIONS:
   - Vb = 12 × (2.2 / 12.2) = 2.16 V
   - Ve = Vb – 0.7 V = 1.46 V
   - Ie = Ve / Re = 3.1 mA
   - Gain Av ≈ -Rc/Re = -4.7

3. RESULT:
   Signal amplified ~4.7 times, inverted phase. Stable operation.
